(* ddi_vol1_corpus.m -- the integrals of S. Blake, "Diabolically Difficult
   Integrals", Volume 1, transcribed for tools/ddi_stress.py, a stress test of
   Integrate[f, x, Method -> "Trager"] and Method -> "ParallelMixedTower" with
   FriCAS as a third opinion.  Results: ALGEBRAIC_INTEGRAL_PERF.md.

   FORMAT.  One case per line:  {"id", "family", "integrand", "expect", "ref"}
   - family: the book chapter (the LaTeX file stem).
   - integrand: a STRING in x.  Integers, x, parameters (single lowercase
     letters a b c d e k m n p q r s t), + - * / ^ ( ), Sqrt[], Log[], Exp[],
     Sin[], Cos[], Tan[], ArcTan[]; every product written with '*', so the
     tool's FriCAS converter is a token rewrite.
   - expect: "elem" / "nonelem" when the book (problem, hint or solution)
     states it, else "".
   - ref: the book problem.
   Parametric integrals appear twice: symbolically, and with the parameters
   instantiated to small integers (id suffix -inst; default a=2, b=3, c=5,
   d=7), so the Q-only Trager implementation is exercised on every problem.
   Families over n are expanded at the listed n.  Skipped: definite
   integrals, non-integration exercises, ArcSin/ArcCsc integrands, general
   templates without a concrete integrand. *)

